    <string name="msp_settings_about_link_failed">Could not open a browser: %1$s</string>

    <!--
      Body of the \"what's new\" dialog. **Update this on every release, in all three
      language files.** `\n` is a line break; lines starting with a bullet are laid out as items.
    -->
    <string name="msp_settings_about_whats_new_body">This release fixes \"subtitles are out of sync\" from two directions at once: an embedded track is now pre-read in full, and subtitles can be nudged proportionally.\n\n· Full read-ahead of an embedded subtitle track: the text track inside the container is read end to end as soon as you open a file, so every line is there immediately (no more waiting for playback to reach a line before it exists). The read never blocks playback, and when it cannot be done the app falls back to reading along with playback\n· Subtitle rate (proportional nudging): five presets (0.96x / 0.98x / 1.00x / 1.02x / 1.04x) plus fine ±0.01 / ±0.10 steps, covering 0.90x-1.10x. It is not the same thing as the timeline offset: that one is a shift, this one is a scale, and it is what you want when the drift grows towards the end (switching files returns it to 1.00x)\n· Reworked lyrics space on the audio page: in portrait the artwork shrinks first when space runs short (below 32dp it is not drawn at all, the lyrics keep a 200dp floor), and once the lyrics viewport drops below 260dp its own padding tightens; in landscape, wide enough windows (>= 711dp) move the feature chips and transport controls into the left column under the artwork, leaving the whole right column to the lyrics\n· A failed pre-read is not an error: the panel just says \"Could not pre-read subtitles, rate adjustment may be off\" (the specific reason goes to the log), it says \"Pre-reading subtitles...\" while it runs, and network streams and bitmap subtitles are reported as not applicable\n· Three problems that only showed up on a real device: every pre-read timestamp was doubled (a line from second 23 played at second 46), the pre-read flooded the log (4085 byte-accounting warnings), and the landscape layout test flipped back and forth at 1220dp because of floating point\n· Earlier: 0.7.0-alpha.2 embedded-subtitle wording fixes, 0.7.0-alpha.1 in-app update checks (GitHub Releases), 0.6.8 background keep-alive, 0.6.7 permissions page and the first-launch permission request, 0.6.6 more translation models (Hunyuan HY-MT2-1.8B added), 0.6.5 cloud speech-to-subtitle\n\nKnown limits: bitmap subtitle formats (PGS / VobSub / DVB) still do not show up and the app does not explain why (planned for 0.9.0); pre-reading walks the whole file in order (network streams are never pre-read and a very large file takes a while); no 32-bit native libraries.</string>

