    <!-- ===== Per-setting help ===== -->

    <string name="msp_settings_help_icon_desc">%1$s: view help</string>

    <string name="msp_settings_force_software_help">By default the playback core picks the decoder: when the system decoder cannot play a file or decodes it wrongly, it switches to the built-in FFmpeg on its own. Turn this on only for a garbled picture, wrong colours or out-of-sync audio and video (a faulty hardware decoder); the cost is noticeably higher battery drain and heat.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_default_aspect_help">Only affects files opened later. A ratio picked for one file in the player applies to that playthrough only and is not saved here.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_default_speed_help">Kept across files: changing the speed in the player changes this too. Long-press speed is a separate setting and is not affected.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_remember_position_help">With this off, every file starts from the beginning. Positions already remembered are not deleted; turning it back on makes them available again.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_record_recent_help">With this off, no new play history is recorded. Resume positions are controlled separately by Remember playback position. What is already recorded is not deleted and reappears when you turn this back on.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_base_url_help">A URL ending in /v1 gets /chat/completions appended automatically. Point this at your own proxy if you use one, as long as its API is OpenAI-compatible.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_test_help">The test really translates one sample line. It verifies the URL, the key, the model name and whether the vendor accepts the request format this app sends, at the cost of a tiny number of tokens.</string>
    <string name="msp_settings_asr_source_help">hf-mirror.com is used by default. Enter https://huggingface.co for the official source; it is usually very slow from mainland China.</string>

